  "_readme": "Curated aircraft-type reference overrides (docs/aircraft-subject-content-plan.md AC5). Applied by scripts/fix-aircraft-types.mjs. Keys are ICAO type designators (DOC 8643). Fields: model (proper marketing name — the restored dump stores family placeholders like '737 Family'), manufacturer (matched by name against the `manufacturers` collection), seats (typical two-class), rangeKm, engines {count,type}, cruiseKts (KNOTS — the dump's `cruiseSpeedKts` column is a mix of km/h and knots, so a curated figure here always wins, no --force-specs needed). Only fields we are confident about are listed; the script fills empty spec fields and replaces a model name only when the stored one is a placeholder. Numbers are typical published figures, not certification data. PUBLIC COPY: mirrored from the Skydex application on every publish; rows under old-dataset alias keys and non-designator keys are omitted here (see data/aliases.json). Propose changes by pull request against THIS file; a maintainer ports merged changes upstream.",
